<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Order of Saints Maurice and Lazarus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1572">1572</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Order of Saints Maurice and Lazarus is a dynastic order of chivalry of the house of Savoy, created in 1572 when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-xiii">Pope Gregory XIII</a> merged the Order of Saint Maurice with the Order of Saint Lazarus at the request of Duke Emmanuel Philibert. It became a leading order of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> and then of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, and is still conferred by the head of the house of Savoy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/order-of-saints-maurice-and-lazarus.jpg" alt="Order of Saints Maurice and Lazarus" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alexeinikolayevichromanov · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GC_SSML_AEACollections.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
